      "@type": "cat-harness:Tool",
      "description": "Gather a release's files from a full Publisher build (package.tgz and its R4/R4B variants, and ast-data.zip, the IG's AST with the Libraries' ELM), say from sushi-config.yaml whether it is a pre-release, and make or refresh the GitHub DRAFT release for the tag with the files uploaded. The owner publishes the draft; a published release is never changed. `check` is the catch-up the AST refresh of the default branch runs (advisory): it reports a current version with no `v<version>` tag, naming the commit that set it for the owner to tag, and a tag with no release, for the owner to run `ig-release.yml` by hand. It never tags and never releases: the tag is the owner's governance step (`ig-release.bpmn`).",
      "install": {
        "none": true
      },
